WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.637
Programs stall low on CISA's maturity
model because they read it as a

2
00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:09.788
five-pillar shopping list: identity,
devices, networks, applications and data.

3
00:00:09.788 --> 00:00:14.666
But the model runs those pillars through
three cross-cutting capabilities, and the

4
00:00:14.666 --> 00:00:19.687
one programs fund least is governance:
defining and enforcing policy across pillars.

5
00:00:19.687 --> 00:00:22.000
No single pillar's tool delivers that.

6
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.950
Three failure patterns recur.

7
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:26.437
Pillars are administered, not governed.

8
00:00:26.437 --> 00:00:30.444
Evidence is shaped by each tool
rather than by the claim it supports,

9
00:00:30.444 --> 00:00:32.876
so every assessment starts from scratch.

10
00:00:32.876 --> 00:00:36.400
And drift is found at audit
time, months after it opened.

11
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.975
The book's answer rests
on a few principles.

12
00:00:38.975 --> 00:00:42.634
Identity is the anchor, but
it isn't self-authenticating,

13
00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:46.850
so sessions are re-evaluated and
the identity plane is defended.

14
00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:49.738
Privileged identity gets
controls of its own.

15
00:00:49.738 --> 00:00:53.025
Evidence must be reproducible
and machine-readable.

16
00:00:53.025 --> 00:00:56.087
And governance must
enforce, not only observe.

17
00:00:56.087 --> 00:01:00.662
A policy whose only consequence is
next quarter's finding is a report.

18
00:01:00.662 --> 00:01:04.913
The decision is the CISO's, with
identity engineering, this quarter:

19
00:01:04.913 --> 00:01:08.934
time-box privileged access,
including the assessment accounts,

20
00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:12.501
and convert one detective
control into a preventive one.

21
00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:16.808
Microsoft's own guidance is zero
permanently active admin assignments,

22
00:01:16.808 --> 00:01:21.762
other than emergency accounts that are
monitored and tested at least every 90 days.

23
00:01:21.762 --> 00:01:24.480
Next, what the mandates actually require.
